diff --git a/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md b/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
index 59d80d28fe3562e531545045fcce310208841234..7b516c113826d624f52df012459b3ea3106c5b48 100644
--- a/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
@@ -99,3 +99,24 @@ negotiation, mixed fitting/oversized response batches, transient pressure with
 exactly one callback after retry, genuine local callback failure, and two live
 connections sharing an action queue through terminal-target cleanup. These are
 connection lifecycle checks; nine-node native quorum acceptance is separate.
+
+Authenticated response ownership now has explicit Applied, Ignored, Rejected and
+LocalFailure outcomes. A valid signature whose `{node, round}` query has already
+expired is consumed as Ignored without changing poll ownership, vote confidence
+or calling the chain apply callback. Unknown queries alone do not immediately
+close healthy peers, matching pinned ABC's poor-network tolerance. Malformed
+signatures, vote counts and vote hashes still reject the peer; local apply or
+snapshot failures remain owner failures.
+
+Pinned ABC's per-connection abuse policy is retained: the first 12 such faults
+have no score, later faults add 2, and a score above 100 rejects the peer. Thus
+62 consecutive authenticated unknown replies remain tolerated and the 63rd is
+terminal. An Applied reply after strictly more than one quiet hour resets the
+fault count; accumulated score remains. Peer counters are bounded and never
+persisted. Tests cover the exact threshold, quiet-count reset with score
+retention, preserved authenticated bindings and the local-failure distinction.
+The poll test separately expires a real query through Next, verifies the actual
+signed late response is Ignored with unchanged native VoteRecord confidence,
+then checks bad signatures/content still reject and future polling remains
+possible. This repairs an upstream semantic mismatch; it does not establish
+that late replies caused the prior nine-node finality deadline failure.
